00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.535
So why analyze your cloud costs?

00:01:52.535 --> 00:01:53.910
I think the first
reason is going

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.660
to be pretty self-explanatory.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.920
Costs are directly tied to
revenue of your business.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:03.410
It's a bit of a
delicate equation here.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:07.670
And the most important part
is costs do sometimes go up.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.340
But if costs go
up, you also have

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.120
to make sure that income is
going up on par or preferably

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.370
at a faster pace than costs.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:17.870
This is going to be critical
to your overall business,

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:19.960
but it's also crucial
for each business

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:23.510
unit and each team that
contributes to these costs.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:26.080
So providing these
business metrics,

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.590
not only to CFOs,
CIOs, et cetera,

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.110
but also to those teams who
are engineering and building

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:35.870
these solutions is
pretty powerful.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:40.610
Second is usage is directly tied
to costs in the cloud world.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.070
With on-prem environments,
truthfully, it

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.600
was a little bit
easier to manage

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.670
costs, because you
bought one server,

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.120
and that server essentially
cost roughly the same

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.100
whether you were
at 0% utilization

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.750
or 100% utilization.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.760
And so when you wanted
your app to scale,

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.210
you were really bound by that
single server or x number

00:02:59.210 --> 00:02:59.927
of servers.

00:02:59.927 --> 00:03:02.510
And if you had wished it could
multiply into multiple servers,

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.370
it just didn't have
that capability.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.020
With cloud, things
operate differently,

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:08.630
differently in a good way.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:12.950
By things like auto scaling, by
being able to click and deploy

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.290
new server instances,
you can essentially

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.660
grow your application from
one server to 10 to 100

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.380
to 1,000 in seconds and minutes.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.250
But there is a
slight caveat there

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.910
in that usage is tied to
cost and that as you use more

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.830
resources, your costs increase.

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.380
So much more important
in this environment

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.600
to actually keep
an eye on how much

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.240
your resources are
costing you and be

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.610
able to kind of turn
that dial and adjust

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.460
as you need the amount of
resources that you have

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:44.980
and the amount of costs that are
contributing to your business.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.820
Third thing is being in control.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:50.290
So by moderating your
costs, you are the point

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.270
of control for your business.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.220
You can determine
how much you're

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.800
spending on GCE, for
instance, and how that's

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.690
contributing to your business.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:01.870
You can keep track of what one
business unit is contributing

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.760
to a business versus
another business unit,

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.290
one team versus
another team, one

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.778
individual versus another
individual, et cetera.

00:04:07.778 --> 00:04:09.820
Potentially, who's running
all those select stars

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:12.470
in your business.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.970
And fourth thing is
being intelligent.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:19.709
So the saying goes that data
is the new oil, the new gold,

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:20.680
et cetera.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:21.589
And that's very true.

00:04:21.589 --> 00:04:23.480
The more data you
gather, the more

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.350
that you can actually
do with that data.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:29.927
So by actually collecting
that data, by gathering it,

00:04:29.927 --> 00:04:32.510
you can do more advanced things,
like building dashboards that

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:35.200
compare your costs to your KPIs,
which we'll be going through

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.400
during this session.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.180
But you can also do
more advanced things

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:41.330
like building ML models to
predict what your costs might

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:44.600
be in the future, or of building
ML models to potentially

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.570
predict where you need to
focus your efforts on product

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:50.110
XYZ or widget ABC, et cetera.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:58.460
And most importantly, you
will inevitably save money.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:01.207
So by actually
monitoring your costs,

00:05:01.207 --> 00:05:03.040
you will be able to
keep track of your costs

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:06.355
and be able to tweak those
spending habits over time.

00:05:06.355 --> 00:05:08.230
So I don't know if you've
done this yourself,

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.050
but a couple of years back
I started more thoroughly

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:15.460
analyzing my personal finances
and was totally shocked

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.780
to find out how much the
occasional $5 cup of coffee

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.280
or the occasional dinner out
with friends et cetera actually

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.240
ended up costing me at
the end of the month.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.750
And so by keeping
an eye on that,

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.630
tracking that, and actually
tailoring my spending habits,

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:32.680
I ended up saving roughly about
10% per month in, once again,

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.480
my personal friends finances.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.430
So by actually
just keeping an eye

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:39.910
and monitoring your spend
costs, you will inevitably

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:42.700
end up saving money.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:45.490
So let's take an example.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:48.540
Let's say that I just open
up a new, exciting bike share

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:51.240
